# Irregular parts on a 1200 x 1200 mm plate with 1 mm between them.
#
#   poly <id> <quantity> <angles>   angles: list like 0,90 or every:<step>
#   ring <vertex-count> <x> <y> ...  first ring is the outline, rest are holes
#
sheet 1200 1200
cell 1.0
clearance 1.0

# An L shape, offered at all four quarter turns.
poly 1 4 every:90
ring 6  0 0  300 0  300 80  120 80  120 200  0 200

# A triangle, upright or upside down.
poly 2 5 0,180
ring 3  0 0  220 0  110 190

# A square frame. Its hole is ordinary free space, so anything small enough
# may end up cut from inside it.
poly 3 2 0
ring 4  0 0  200 0  200 200  0 200
ring 4  60 60  140 60  140 140  60 140

# A part at an angle no axis-aligned packer could use.
poly 4 3 every:90
ring 5  0 0  180 0  180 60  90 130  0 60

# Plain rectangles still work; they are polygons underneath.
rect 5  6  140 90 1
rect 6 10   70 55 1
